WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:18.964
Meanwhile, back in the town of Oliver's birth, Mr. Bumble was about to set off on a trip to London.

2
00:00:18.965 --> 00:00:25.726
He was feeling quite important this morning because the workhouse board had appointed him to take two paupers to the city.

3
00:00:25.727 --> 00:00:30.202
He was going to appear before a court to argue that they belonged to another parish.

4
00:00:30.203 --> 00:00:36.028
So Mr. Bumble took his place on top of the coach, accompanied by the two men in their ragged clothes.

5
00:00:36.029 --> 00:00:41.131
Throughout the trip the paupers persisted in shivering and complaining about the cold.

6
00:00:41.132 --> 00:00:48.695
This annoyed Mr. Bumble and made his teeth chatter even though he was wearing a heavy coat. By evening they reached London.

7
00:00:48.696 --> 00:00:55.361
Having disposed of the paupers in a workhouse for the night, Mr. Bumble settled himself at a warm and cozy inn.

8
00:00:55.362 --> 00:01:00.599
He had a modest dinner of steaks, oyster sauce, and fine wine.

9
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:05.369
After dinner he set a drink on the mantel and pulled his chair over to the fire.

10
00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:09.202
Then he composed himself for an evening of reading the newspaper.

11
00:01:09.203 --> 00:01:13.790
The very first paragraph on which his eye rested was the following advertisement:

12
00:01:13.814 --> 00:01:16.187
FIVE POUNDS REWARD

13
00:01:16.187 --> 00:01:25.424
A young boy named Oliver Twist ran away, or was enticed away, from his home last Thursday. He has not been seen or heard from since.

14
00:01:25.425 --> 00:01:32.003
The above reward will be paid to any person who gives information that leads to the discovery of Oliver Twist.

15
00:01:32.004 --> 00:01:37.908
The above reward is also offered to anyone who can throw light on the boy's previous history.

16
00:01:37.909 --> 00:01:42.575
The advertiser has many reasons for being interested in the boy's past.

17
00:01:42.576 --> 00:01:53.241
Mr. Bumble opened his eyes in surprise. There followed a full description of Oliver's clothing and appearance, with Mr. Brownlow's name and address underneath.

18
00:01:53.242 --> 00:01:57.979
Mr. Bumble read the advertisement slowly and carefully three times.

19
00:01:57.980 --> 00:02:05.058
And in something more than five minutes, he was on his way to Mr. Brownlow's house, having left his drink untasted on the mantel.

20
00:02:05.059 --> 00:02:10.384
"Is Mr. Brownlow at home?" inquired Mr. Bumble of the servant girl who opened the door.

21
00:02:10.385 --> 00:02:17.138
The girl replied as any good servant would: "I don't know, sir. What is the nature of your business with him?"

22
00:02:17.139 --> 00:02:22.281
Mr. Bumble explained that he had come in reference to the advertisement about Oliver Twist.

23
00:02:22.282 --> 00:02:28.789
Hearing that, Mrs. Bedwin, who had been standing at the parlor door, hurried into the hall in a breathless state.

24
00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:38.210
"Come in, come in," said the old woman. "I knew we would hear of him. Poor dear! I knew we would.

25
00:02:38.211 --> 00:02:44.186
I was certain of it. Bless his heart. I said so all along."

26
00:02:44.187 --> 00:02:48.686
Having said this, the housekeeper hurried back into the parlor again.

27
00:02:48.687 --> 00:02:52.257
She sat down on the sofa and burst into tears.

28
00:02:52.258 --> 00:02:58.599
Meanwhile the girl had run upstairs and now returned with a request that Mr. Bumble follow her immediately.

29
00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:01.932
She showed him upstairs into Mr. Brownlow's study.

30
00:03:01.933 --> 00:03:09.353
"Take a seat, will you?" said Mr. Brownlow. He moved the lamp so as to obtain a good view of Mr. Bumble's face.

31
00:03:09.354 --> 00:03:13.916
"Now, sir, you have come as a result of seeing the newspaper advertisement?"

32
00:03:13.917 --> 00:03:17.408
"Yes, sir," said Mr. Bumble as he took a seat.

33
00:03:17.409 --> 00:03:23.813
"Do you know where this poor boy is now?" asked Mr. Brownlow with a look of deep concern on his face.

34
00:03:23.814 --> 00:03:25.916
"No, I don't."

35
00:03:25.917 --> 00:03:33.749
"Then what do you know of him?" Mr. Brownlow said impatiently. "Please tell me what you know about Oliver as quickly as possible."

36
00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:40.662
Mr. Bumble put down his hat, unbuttoned his coat, folded his arms, and bowed his head in a thoughtful manner.

37
00:03:40.663 --> 00:03:44.146
After a few moments of reflection, he began his story.

38
00:03:44.147 --> 00:03:48.146
"I am the parish officer at the workhouse where Oliver was born.

39
00:03:48.147 --> 00:03:52.892
Young Oliver was an orphan, the son of low and vicious parents.

40
00:03:52.893 --> 00:03:57.725
Despite a large reward, we have never been able to determine their names.

41
00:03:57.726 --> 00:04:04.948
From the moment of his birth, Oliver displayed no better qualities than treachery, ingratitude, and malice."

42
00:04:04.949 --> 00:04:09.122
Here Mr. Bumble paused to let his words sink in.

43
00:04:09.123 --> 00:04:16.281
Mr. Brownlow said nothing, but he looked very serious. "Go on," he said to the parish officer.

44
00:04:16.282 --> 00:04:25.281
"Oliver was apprenticed to an undertaker, a position that any boy would be happy and grateful for. But was he grateful? No.

45
00:04:25.282 --> 00:04:33.193
He viciously attacked a defenseless boy who was also employed there, and he terrorized the undertaker's wife and a female servant.

46
00:04:33.194 --> 00:04:39.256
Young Twist knew that he deserved a most horrible punishment. So what do you think he did?"

47
00:04:39.257 --> 00:04:44.852
"I don't know," said Mr. Brownlow, who at this point was feeling that he didn't know Oliver at all.

48
00:04:44.853 --> 00:04:51.590
"He ran away from his master's house. So, you see, he has a history of running away."

49
00:04:51.591 --> 00:05:00.574
"I fear that what you say is true." Mr. Brownlow shook his head sadly. He handed a five-pound note to Mr. Bumble.

50
00:05:00.575 --> 00:05:08.646
"This is not much for your information. I would gladly have given you three times as much money if your report had been favorable to the boy."

51
00:05:08.647 --> 00:05:16.050
If only Mr. Bumble had known that! He might have presented his little history with a very different slant.

52
00:05:16.051 --> 00:05:21.725
It was too late to do that now, however, so he shook his head gravely and pocketed the money.

53
00:05:21.726 --> 00:05:26.637
After Mr. Bumble left, Mr. Brownlow paced the room for a few minutes.

54
00:05:26.638 --> 00:05:33.709
He was very disturbed by the parish officer's tale. At last he stopped and rang the bell violently.

55
00:05:33.710 --> 00:05:40.209
"Mrs. Bedwin," said Mr. Brownlow, when the housekeeper appeared. "That boy Oliver is an impostor."

56
00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:45.955
"It can't be, sir. It cannot be," insisted the housekeeper.

57
00:05:45.956 --> 00:05:50.114
"What do you mean by that?" retorted Mr. Brownlow.

58
00:05:50.115 --> 00:05:58.939
"I tell you he is an impostor. I have just heard a full account of him from birth. He has been a thorough villain all his life."

59
00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:07.034
"I never will believe it," Mrs. Bedwin replied indignantly. "He was a dear, grateful, gentle child, sir."

60
00:06:07.035 --> 00:06:15.034
"Silence!" ordered Mr. Brownlow. "Never let me hear the boy's name again. I rang to tell you that.

61
00:06:15.035 --> 00:06:23.336
Never, never, on any pretense. You may leave the room, Mrs. Bedwin. Remember, I am in earnest about this."

62
00:06:23.337 --> 00:06:26.844
There were sad hearts at Mr. Brownlow's house that night.

63
00:06:26.845 --> 00:06:31.931
Although Mr. Brownlow sounded angry, he was more disappointed than truly angry.

64
00:06:31.932 --> 00:06:37.415
Back at Fagin's house, Oliver's heart sank whenever he thought of his warm, kind friends.

65
00:06:37.416 --> 00:06:41.177
It was a good thing that he did not know what they had heard that day.

66
00:06:41.178 --> 00:06:47.719
If he had known about Mr. Bumble's words, his heart might have broken completely.
